DavidLNorris/status/1752881807324758475\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T02:29:24Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>retweet</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752881972123230345":{"a":"<p>RT @RocketLab: Nine Rutherford engines launched to space, nine safely back on Earth after a quick swim 🔥 🌊 t.co</p>\n\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1752781842393276652\">https://x.com/i/status/1752781842393276652</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752881972123230345\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752881972123230345</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1752881972123230345</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752881972123230345\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T02:30:03Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>retweet</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752885564095803776":{"a":"<p>I think this decision is just a test of how flawed the system really is. Elon worked his ass off for that money and seems to know how to spend it well. Regardless of his whacky behavior and crazy friends I do not comprehend this dispute in any way. I am curious to see resolution. <a href=\"https://x.com/andrewrsorkin/status/1752872326536831064\">Tweet by @andrewrsorkin</a></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/andrewrsorkin/status/1752872326536831064\">https://x.com/andrewrsorkin/status/1752872326536831064</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1752885564095803776</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752885564095803776\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T02:44:20Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752890487562785072":{"a":"<p>Looking at photos and found this before and after of this root bin. It was a little rough. I added a piece of molding for a chalk ledge and sprayed a little chalkboard paint on the front. New plexi+art, bottom covered in vinyl and the hinges were cleaned and painted with enamel. t.co</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752890487562785072\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752890487562785072</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1752890487562785072</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752890487562785072\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T03:03:54Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752891870949093873":{"a":"<p>Instead of buying a new motor I foolishly repaired this one after like 13 people said it was impossible. PETG FDM 3D Print on the shaft end and high temp resin SLA 3D print to hold the brushes. The PETG was getting soft and letting the bearing slip on the brush side at low speed. t.co</p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOFUGBXQAA8sAK.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOFUHhWcAAoQyn.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOFUJGWYAAKwnv.png\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOFULMXYAADj-8.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>","m":"<h1>Post 1752891870949093873</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752891870949093873\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T03:09:23Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>thread</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>thread_count</dt><dd>8</dd><dt>conversation</dt><dd>1752891870949093873</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752892927464907210":{"a":"<p>Factory motor was not meant for the abuse of a lathe. My mods to the design made it indestructible but returned the motor to the correct geometry for the rest of the lathe. They had done some weird things to make the wrong motor fit. Here&#x27;s the bracket I had to design and make: t.co</p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOGzvhXcAAVqSG.png\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOGzviWkAE6el4.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\" data-conversation=\"none\" data-dnt=\"true\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1752891870949093873\">https://x.com/i/status/1752891870949093873</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1752892927464907210</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752892927464907210\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T03:13:35Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>thread</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>thread_count</dt><dd>8</dd><dt>conversation</dt><dd>1752891870949093873</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752894886104191249":{"a":"<p>Transferring the brush holders from the cast metal to the resin was a mess. You can see that the metal casting wasn&#x27;t properly fired. Still powered metal inside. t.co</p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOImPeWIAAExsc.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOImPfXsAATfbr.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOImPgXkAANNK6.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOImPiWkAAG9Eu.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\" data-conversation=\"none\" data-dnt=\"true\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1752892927464907210\">https://x.com/i/status/1752892927464907210</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1752894886104191249</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752894886104191249\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T03:21:22Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>thread</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>thread_count</dt><dd>8</dd><dt>conversation</dt><dd>1752891870949093873</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752895898487595288":{"a":"<p>Brush holders are now held in with RTV silicone.If you design everything right there are no fitment issues. No alignment to do. 3D printing is great for that. CNC usually as well though the violence of the process can introduce odd errors. I had to glue the metal one to a napkin…</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\" data-conversation=\"none\" data-dnt=\"true\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1752894886104191249\">https://x.com/i/status/1752894886104191249</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1752895898487595288</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752895898487595288\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T03:25:24Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>thread</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>thread_count</dt><dd>8</dd><dt>conversation</dt><dd>1752891870949093873</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752896581160816869":{"a":"<p>We needed a way to switch the high CFM vacuum motor on the laser cutter. I whipped this up in Fusion 360 from a NEMA box model and used 3D models of the parts as tools to cut out perfect holes. Or I could have driven to the store or ordered something and waited. 30 cents or so. t.co</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752896581160816869\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752896581160816869</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1752896581160816869</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752896581160816869\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T03:28:06Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752897333363196235":{"a":"<p>It would have taken hours to punch those holes by hand in a real NEMA box I didn&#x27;t really need; but thats the only thing safe I could likely buy and 100 times the cost. The end product would&#x27;ve looked like crap. This is pretty perfect. 3D printing isn&#x27;t for everything but this...</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1752896581160816869\">https://x.com/i/status/1752896581160816869</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1752897333363196235</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752897333363196235\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T03:31:06Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752897796565311902":{"a":"<p>Grandma says &quot;Fix yer sh...&quot; and stop buying new crap that is inferior to the old stuff you threw away. t.co</p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOLPznWkAAEIRB.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>","m":"<h1>Post 1752897796565311902</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752897796565311902\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T03:32:56Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>thread</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>thread_count</dt><dd>7</dd><dt>conversation</dt><dd>1752897796565311902</dd>\n</dl>"},"1752898555793080760":{"a":"<p>Grandpa says, &quot;And build some new shi... nobody seen before. Hold my beer and watch this...&quot; t.co</p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GFOLzbKXMAAmBKH.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>","m":"<h1>Post 1752898555793080760</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1752898555793080760\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-01T03:35:57Z</dd><dt